Q: how to send Notification to mobile device using PHP cURL and FCM? A: <p>The legacy FCM API has been deprecated. This answer covers the <strong>HTTP v1 API</strong> using a <strong>Service Account</strong> for authentication.</p>
<p>Step 1: Create a Firebase Service Account</p>
<ol>
<li><p>Go to <a href="https://console.firebase.google.com/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Firebase Console</a></p>
</li>
<li><p>Navigate to <strong>Project Settings</strong> → <strong>Service Accounts</strong></p>
</li>
<li><p>Click <strong>&quot;Generate new private key&quot;</strong> → Download the JSON file</p>
</li>
<li><p>Save it securely (e.g., <code>service-account.json</code>) — <strong>never commit this to version control</strong></p>
</li>
</ol>
<p>Step 2: Install the JWT Library</p>
<p>You need firebase/php-jwt to sign the OAuth2 token request.</p>
<p><code>composer require firebase/php-jwt</code></p>
<p>Or if not using Composer, clone it manually:</p>
<p><code>git clone https://github.com/firebase/php-jwt.git firebase/jwt</code></p>
<p>Step 3: Define Your Service Account Path</p>
<p><code>define('USER_ACCOUNT_KEYFILE', __DIR__ . '/service-account.json');</code></p>
<p>Step 4: Get OAuth2 Access Token</p>
<p>This function reads your service account credentials and exchanges a signed JWT for a short-lived Bearer token.</p>
<pre><code>function getFireAccessToken()
{
    require_once 'firebase/jwt/vendor/autoload.php';

    $keyFile = USER_ACCOUNT_KEYFILE;
    $keyData = json_decode(file_get_contents($keyFile), true);

    $clientEmail = $keyData['client_email'];
    $privateKey  = $keyData['private_key'];
    $scopes      = ['https://www.googleapis.com/auth/cloud-platform'];

    $now   = time();
    $token = [
        'iss'   =&gt; $clientEmail,
        'scope' =&gt; implode(' ', $scopes),
        'aud'   =&gt; 'https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token',
        'exp'   =&gt; $now + 3600,
        'iat'   =&gt; $now
    ];

    $jwtToken = \Firebase\JWT\JWT::encode($token, $privateKey, 'RS256');

    $ch = curl_init();
    curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_URL, 'https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token');
    curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_RETURNTRANSFER, 1);
    curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_POST, 1);
    curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_POSTFIELDS, http_build_query([
        'grant_type' =&gt; 'urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:jwt-bearer',
        'assertion'  =&gt; $jwtToken
    ]));

    $response     = curl_exec($ch);
    curl_close($ch);
    $responseData = json_decode($response, true);

    return $responseData['access_token'] ?? null;
}
</code></pre>
<p>Step 5: Send the Push Notification</p>
<p>Replace YOUR_PROJECT_ID with your Firebase project ID (found in Project Settings).</p>
<pre><code>function sendfirenotification($to, $title, $message, $img = &quot;&quot;, $datapayload = [], $multiple = false)
{
    $projectId = 'YOUR_PROJECT_ID'; // 🔴 Replace this

    $notification = [
        'title' =&gt; $title,
        'body'  =&gt; $message,
    ];

    if ($img) {
        $notification['image'] = $img;
    }

    if (!empty($datapayload)) {
        // FCM 'data' payload values must all be strings
        $notification['custom'] = $datapayload;
    }

    $fields = [
        'message' =&gt; [
            'notification' =&gt; $notification,
            'android' =&gt; [
                'notification' =&gt; ['sound' =&gt; 'default']
            ],
            'apns' =&gt; [
                'payload' =&gt; [
                    'aps' =&gt; [
                        'mutable-content' =&gt; 1,
                        'sound'           =&gt; 'default'
                    ]
                ]
            ],
            'data' =&gt; array_map('strval', $datapayload) // data fields must be strings
        ]
    ];

    // Single token vs multiple tokens (multicast)
    $fields['message'][$multiple ? 'tokens' : 'token'] = $to;

    $accessToken = getFireAccessToken();

    if (!$accessToken) {
        return json_encode(['status' =&gt; false, 'msg' =&gt; 'Failed to retrieve access token.']);
    }

    $url = &quot;https://fcm.googleapis.com/v1/projects/{$projectId}/messages:send&quot;;

    $ch = curl_init();
    curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_URL,            $url);
    curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_POST,           true);
    curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_HTTPHEADER,     [
        'Authorization: Bearer ' . $accessToken,
        'Content-Type: application/json'
    ]);
    curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_RETURNTRANSFER, true);
    curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYPEER, false); // Set true in production
    curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_POSTFIELDS,     json_encode($fields));

    $result = curl_exec($ch);
    curl_close($ch);

    return json_encode([
        'request'  =&gt; $fields,
        'response' =&gt; json_decode($result, true)
    ]);
}
</code></pre>
<p>Step 6: Usage</p>
<pre><code>// Single device
$result = sendfirenotification(
    &quot;DEVICE_FCM_TOKEN&quot;,
    &quot;Test Notification&quot;,
    &quot;Hello from PHP!&quot;,
    &quot;https://www.google.co.in/images/branding/googleg/1x/googleg_standard_color_128dp.png&quot;,
    [&quot;ID&quot; =&gt; &quot;1&quot;]  // Note: data values should be strings
);

echo $result;

// Multiple devices (multicast)
$tokens = [&quot;TOKEN_1&quot;, &quot;TOKEN_2&quot;, &quot;TOKEN_3&quot;];
$result = sendfirenotification(
    $tokens,
    &quot;Broadcast&quot;,
    &quot;Hello everyone!&quot;,
    &quot;&quot;,
    [],
    true // $multiple = true
);

echo $result;
</code></pre>

